"comparison": "Both JPMorgan and Bank of America are subject to the Federal Reserve's CCAR framework and stress testing requirements that determine their Stress Capital Buffer (SCB). JPMorgan discloses the general process where the Fed uses severely adverse scenario results to determine the SCB requirement for the coming year, noting the filing deadline for its annual CCAR submission. Similarly, Bank of America states that the Federal Reserve conducts stress testing on parts of its business using hypothetical economic scenarios prepared by the Fed, and that these scenarios may affect CCAR stress test results which impact the level of its SCB.",
